## 📂 Project Structure
Resume analyser/
│
├── app.py # Main Streamlit application
│
├── data/
│ ├── ResumeDataSet.csv # Training dataset
│ └── analysis_data.ipynb # Data analysis notebook
│
├── models/
│ ├── vectorizer.pkl # TF-IDF vectorizer
│ ├── encoding labels.pkl # Encoded label mapping
│ └── KNC model.pkl # Trained K-Nearest Neighbors model
│
├── preprocess/
│ ├── clean_data.py # Text cleaning and preprocessing
│ └── vectorization.py # Text vectorization logic
│
├── models/
│ └── saving needed models and files
│
├── train/
│ ├── train_model.py # Model training script
│ └── deploy_pipeline.py # Prediction pipeline
│
├── README.md
│
└── requirements.txt

🚀 Usage

Launch the Streamlit app.

Upload a resume file (.pdf).

Wait a few seconds for the system to analyze and classify it.

View the predicted job domain and other extracted information.

🧬 Model Details

Algorithm: K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)

Vectorization: TF-IDF

Preprocessing: Stopword removal, punctuation cleaning, tokenization

Training Data: 2400+ labeled resumes across multiple job domains

🔮 Future Improvements

Add Named Entity Recognition (NER) for skill extraction.

Integrate deep learning models (e.g., BERT) for better accuracy.

Enable batch processing of multiple resumes.

Add visualization dashboards for HR insights.

Deploy the app on the web (e.g., Streamlit Cloud / Heroku / AWS).

